            "n_events": 34,
            "result_text": "Done! I've saved the regex pattern to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nThe pattern works as follows:\n\n1. **`(?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9])`** — Matches either line start or a non-alphanumeric character before the IP\n2. **IPv4 address** — Validates each octet is 0-255 with no leading zeros, surrounded by non-alphanumeric boundaries\n3. **`.*?`** — Non-greedy match of any characters between IP and date\n4. **`(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])`** — Ensures date isn't preceded by alphanumeric (word boundary check)\n5. **Date capture group** — `(\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01]))`\n6. **`(?![a-zA-Z0-9])`** — Ensures date isn't followed by alphanumeric\n7. **`(?!.*\\d{4}-...(?![a-zA-Z0-9]))`** — Negative lookahead ensuring this is the LAST valid date on the line\n\nWhen used with `re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)`, it returns a list of dates (the captured group) from lines containing valid IPv4 addresses."
        }
